{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:08:02Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 153, "kind": "message", "text": "That's fine \u2014 no test-review.md yet since this is mid-cycle.\n\n## Handoff \u2014 attempt 2 fix for changes-requested\n\n**Fixed the blocking crash** (`frontend/src/App.jsx`), root cause not symptom:\n\n- **Root cause of the crash:** `pendingDeleteIds.map((id) => tasks.find((t) => t.id === id))` looked deleted-task-ids up in `tasks` after the fact. When \"Clear completed\" (or any other refresh) removes a task from `tasks` while it's still mid-undo-window, the lookup returns `undefined`, and `UndoToast.jsx:6`'s `key={task.id}` throws.\n- **Fix:** the toast's `pending` prop is now derived the other way around \u2014 `tasks.filter((t) => pendingDeletes.has(t.id))` (`App.jsx:134`). A `filter` over `tasks` can structurally never produce `undefined` entries, so a task that vanished from `tasks` via any other path is silently excluded from the toast instead of crashing it. Its still-running delete timer fires normally later, hits the existing \"no such task\" 404 handling (`App.jsx:85-91`, unchanged), and is silently cleaned up \u2014 no new code path needed there.\n- **Also addressed the will-comment item:** collapsed the two always-mutated-together stores (`pendingDeleteIds` state array + `pendingDeleteTimers` ref `Map`) into one `pendingDeletes` state `Map<id, timerHandle>` (`App.jsx:20-25, 40, 75-103`). This was the duplicate-source-of-truth pattern the reviewer flagged as the kind of thing that produces desync bugs like the one above \u2014 collapsing it removes the spot a future edit would need to remember to touch twice. `useRef` import dropped since it's no longer used.\n\n**Files changed:** only `frontend/src/App.jsx`. `UndoToast.jsx`, `TaskList.jsx`, `api.js`, backend \u2014 untouched, as before.\n\n**Verified:**\n- `npm run build` (Vite/esbuild) \u2014 passes clean, no errors.\n- Manually traced the reviewer's exact repro (delete a completed task, then Clear Completed before the 5s window lapses) against the new code: `tasks` loses the task on the Clear Completed refresh \u2192 `pendingDeletes` still has its id \u2192 `tasks.filter(...)` on the next render simply yields one fewer element \u2192 no crash, toast just drops that entry.\n- Could not run `npm test` \u2014 no test script/framework is configured in `frontend/package.json` (only `dev`/`build`/`lint`/`preview`), and this was true before my change too; not something in this scope to add. Could not run `npm run lint` (oxlint) \u2014 the sandbox declined to approve that command in this session with no prompt to retry; build output shows no syntax/type issues in the meantime.\n\nAll six acceptance criteria from `docs/spec.md` remain satisfied \u2014 this fix only changes *how* the pending list is derived, not the delete/undo/timer/multi-undo behavior itself.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "54aa24cf-1f06-4523-975a-4e66b25f56e3"}}
{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:08:02Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 154, "kind": "status", "text": "That's fine \u2014 no test-review.md yet since this is mid-cycle.\n\n## Handoff \u2014 attempt 2 fix for changes-requested\n\n**Fixed the blocking crash** (`frontend/src/App.jsx`), root cause not symptom:\n\n- **Root cause of the crash:** `pendingDeleteIds.map((id) => tasks.find((t) => t.id === id))` looked deleted-task-ids up in `tasks` after the fact. When \"Clear completed\" (or any other refresh) removes a task from `tasks` while it's still mid-undo-window, the lookup returns `undefined`, and `UndoToast.jsx:6`'s `key={task.id}` throws.\n- **Fix:** the toast's `pending` prop is now derived the other way around \u2014 `tasks.filter((t) => pendingDeletes.has(t.id))` (`App.jsx:134`). A `filter` over `tasks` can structurally never produce `undefined` entries, so a task that vanished from `tasks` via any other path is silently excluded from the toast instead of crashing it. Its still-running delete timer fires normally later, hits the existing \"no such task\" 404 handling (`App.jsx:85-91`, unchanged), and is silently cleaned up \u2014 no new code path needed there.\n- **Also addressed the will-comment item:** collapsed the two always-mutated-together stores (`pendingDeleteIds` state array + `pendingDeleteTimers` ref `Map`) into one `pendingDeletes` state `Map<id, timerHandle>` (`App.jsx:20-25, 40, 75-103`). This was the duplicate-source-of-truth pattern the reviewer flagged as the kind of thing that produces desync bugs like the one above \u2014 collapsing it removes the spot a future edit would need to remember to touch twice. `useRef` import dropped since it's no longer used.\n\n**Files changed:** only `frontend/src/App.jsx`. `UndoToast.jsx`, `TaskList.jsx`, `api.js`, backend \u2014 untouched, as before.\n\n**Verified:**\n- `npm run build` (Vite/esbuild) \u2014 passes clean, no errors.\n- Manually traced the reviewer's exact repro (delete a completed task, then Clear Completed before the 5s window lapses) against the new code: `tasks` loses the task on the Clear Completed refresh \u2192 `pendingDeletes` still has its id \u2192 `tasks.filter(...)` on the next render simply yields one fewer element \u2192 no crash, toast just drops that entry.\n- Could not run `npm test` \u2014 no test script/framework is configured in `frontend/package.json` (only `dev`/`build`/`lint`/`preview`), and this was true before my change too; not something in this scope to add. Could not run `npm run lint` (oxlint) \u2014 the sandbox declined to approve that command in this session with no prompt to retry; build output shows no syntax/type issues in the meantime.\n\nAll six acceptance criteria from `docs/spec.md` remain satisfied \u2014 this fix only changes *how* the pending list is derived, not the delete/undo/timer/multi-undo behavior itself.", "meta": {"native_type": "result", "subtype": "success", "session_id": "54aa24cf-1f06-4523-975a-4e66b25f56e3", "is_error": false, "total_cost_usd": 0.8598047999999999}}
